00:43:32.130 --> 00:43:33.210
like the way you communicate

00:43:33.210 --> 00:43:35.190
so I actually think
you've got a shot here,

00:43:35.190 --> 00:43:37.620
whatever great advice Amy's about to give

00:43:37.620 --> 00:43:40.860
I just really want you to
know the answer is content.

00:43:40.860 --> 00:43:44.307
- Calvin, when I wanted to
take speaking seriously I did.

00:43:44.307 --> 00:43:48.500
In 2015 I was like if
anyone allows me to speak

00:43:48.500 --> 00:43:50.300
from an application or asked me to speak

00:43:50.300 --> 00:43:52.380
I'm gonna pay whatever
it takes to get there.

00:43:52.380 --> 00:43:55.050
I went to the Philippines,
I went to Manchester, UK,

00:43:55.050 --> 00:43:59.750
I went everywhere and I spoke
on 15 16, 17 stages that year.

00:43:59.750 --> 00:44:03.400
I spent a lot of money and
travel but I got experience.

00:44:03.400 --> 00:44:05.840
And then what happens,
people watch you on YouTube

00:44:05.840 --> 00:44:07.413
for whatever reason they
think you can talk to

00:44:07.413 --> 00:44:08.750
1,000 people in an audience

00:44:08.750 --> 00:44:10.630
when you're sitting alone in
a bedroom talking to a camera

00:44:10.630 --> 00:44:13.430
but it still worked out,
content in that capacity

00:44:13.430 --> 00:44:15.940
plus actually getting out
and getting experience.

00:44:15.940 --> 00:44:17.810
And then everybody was
like, you gotta write a book

00:44:17.810 --> 00:44:19.424
so that helped.

00:44:19.424 --> 00:44:20.257
- [Calvin] So, I have that piece down

00:44:20.257 --> 00:44:23.478
where I have experience, I've
got to be on some fun stages.

00:44:23.478 --> 00:44:25.570
Spoke in Salt Lake City last year

00:44:25.570 --> 00:44:29.200
with Mel Robbins, Tom Bilyeu,
Jay Shetty and a few others

00:44:29.200 --> 00:44:31.593
but it's just not that much.

00:44:34.564 --> 00:44:37.530
- Do you email every, I emailed
every single tech conference

00:44:37.530 --> 00:44:39.280
when I was doing Wine Library TV

00:44:39.280 --> 00:44:41.140
I emailed every single tech conference

00:44:41.140 --> 00:44:43.790
that I could get on a Google
Alert and emailed them

00:44:43.790 --> 00:44:45.990
and ask them if they
would have me to speak.

00:44:47.040 --> 00:44:49.340
- Okay, so don't annoy you but go ahead

00:44:49.340 --> 00:44:51.710
and just reach out to everybody else

00:44:51.710 --> 00:44:53.060
and that's the way to get in.

00:44:53.060 --> 00:44:54.270
- Or annoy me.

00:44:54.270 --> 00:44:55.660
The game is about asking

00:44:55.660 --> 00:44:57.491
- And at the end of the day like

00:44:57.491 --> 00:45:00.430
there's not gonna be one clear-cut way.

00:45:00.430 --> 00:45:03.190
The loudest person still
wins a lot of the time.

00:45:03.190 --> 00:45:06.050
Like, if they are consistent,
if they're persistent,

00:45:06.050 --> 00:45:07.770
and the one thing that I've always had is

00:45:07.770 --> 00:45:09.060
I've had staying power.

00:45:09.060 --> 00:45:11.520
Like for me if I'm just
talking about me at this point

00:45:11.520 --> 00:45:14.600
I have been producing
content for 10 years.

00:45:14.600 --> 00:45:16.540
I have stuck around, it's not been,

00:45:16.540 --> 00:45:18.020
when are you gonna give up on YouTube?

00:45:18.020 --> 00:45:21.470
I'm not giving up on YouTube
until they give up on the world

00:45:21.470 --> 00:45:23.810
like I'm just gonna keep
doing what I know how to do

00:45:23.810 --> 00:45:25.910
in the best capacity that I know how.

00:45:25.910 --> 00:45:28.130
I promise you, especially now

00:45:28.130 --> 00:45:31.782
where everybody's talking about
how, what's the word, not,

00:45:31.782 --> 00:45:34.770
super busy, super crazy,
the amount of content

00:45:34.770 --> 00:45:37.810
